BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Durham Parks & Recreation
DESCRIPTION:Come along with Outdoor Recreation staff and a member of New Ho
 pe Bird Alliance as we lead a bird outing and birdwatch at a city park. Th
 is is a 3-part series. Each bird outing takes place on a Friday and will o
 ccur at a different city park every week. The birdwatching series is open 
 to all levels of birdwatching experience. Participants are encouraged to b
 ring their own binoculars\, as supplies is limited. Preregistration is req
 uired for all participants. https://www.dprplaymore.org/calendar.aspx?EID=
 6839
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261009T100000
DTSTAMP;TZID=America/New_York:20260918T144058
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261009T080000
LAST-MODIFIED;TZID=America/New_York:20260918T144058
LOCATION:<p>Sandy Creek Park</p> - 3510 Sandy Creek Road  Durham NC 27707
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Fall Birdwatch Series
UID:6839
URL:/common/modules/iCalendar/iCalendar.aspx?feed=calendar&catID=22
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Durham Parks & Recreation
DESCRIPTION:It's time to get out on the trails with your pup! Join us for a
  nature walk along the Eno River where you and your dog can meet new frien
 ds. The hike will stop along the river for dogs that want to cool off. Dog
 s are required to be on a non-retractable leash at all times. Participant 
 registration is required. https://www.dprplaymore.org/calendar.aspx?EID=68
 38
